# QA run history

<!-- trailhead v{{VERSION}} -->

The ledger of QA runs. `scripts/checks/qa-ratchet.mjs` credits a spec as having run when
its name appears here or in a `.qa/reports/` filename — both written by the QA engine,
not by hand, which is what makes the count checkable rather than self-reported.

**Do not edit this file to make the gate green.** The number it produces —
"N of M specs have ever run" — prints on every gate run precisely so the debt cannot be
quietly carried. A project that edits its own ledger has replaced a measurement with a
claim, which is the failure this whole apparatus exists to prevent.

